# Project Rules (Backend only)

## Stack
- Language: Java 17
- Framework: Spring Boot 3 (if applicable)
- Build: Gradle or Maven (use what the repo already uses)
- Database: do not assume; follow existing repository patterns

## Non-negotiables
- Do NOT add new dependencies unless explicitly requested.
- Do NOT change public contracts (public methods, REST endpoints, DTO shapes) unless explicitly requested.
- Do NOT introduce new modules/packages without justification.
- Prefer explicit, readable code over cleverness.

## Output quality
- Changes must be minimal, focused, and PR-friendly.
- Avoid speculative edits across many files.
- If something is unclear, make the smallest safe assumption and state it.

## Privacy / Security
- Never request or output credentials, tokens, API keys, secrets.
- Do not log sensitive data (PII, tokens, passwords).
